eactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T14:23:39-08:00","id":363795,"title":"","content":"That is what I thought, but just wanted to verify.<br /> <br /> I added the table I created in the other thread to my first post in this thread. I'm lazy and wanted to have a quick way to find character names. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T15:51:45-08:00","id":363879,"title":"","content":"I haven't done too many play by post threads. Do we just keep moving forward and create unimportant locations npcs, if needed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-08-2015, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T18:02:38-08:00","id":363957,"title":"","content":"I asked the ST, and apparently it's fine if we invent unimportant locales like the teashop and run minor NPCs/extras using common sense to keep things flowing. We can head out and invent a bar, no worries.<br /> <br /> Don't think we're allowed to invent a bar that hands out complimentary daiklaves to their customers, or invent a spontaneous ninja-attack at said bar-that's ST's job.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Man, playing the lady defending the slave trade is interesting. I need to play more Guild-affiliated PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T18:10:17-08:00","id":363959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/361620-clash-of-the-southeast-ooc?p=363957#post363957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked the ST, and apparently it's fine if we invent unimportant locales like the teashop and run minor NPCs/extras using common sense to keep things flowing. We can head out and invent a bar, no worries.<br /> <br /> Don't think we're allowed to invent a bar that hands out complimentary daiklaves to their customers, or invent a spontaneous ninja-attack at said bar-that's ST's job.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Man, playing the lady defending the slave trade is interesting. I need to play more Guild-affiliated PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is correct. You can invent non-major characters and places. If the character is going to do something that is not basic (like a worker at a tea shop...) I will make them. If you want a bazaar stall that is selling stuff... I decide what wares. You can just say you want to look for a specific one and I will decide if it is there or not. Basically don't create characters that fit your needs. Just have basic ones that would be there whether you want them or not. <br /> <br /> Buildings with specialties might not be there. Things like a bar, bazaar, or tea shop are not uncommon. If I tell you a town is small, I will probably tell you most of the things in it. I will say something like &quot;you imagined that it was a diklaive store until you realized they were all fakes&quot; in the story if you overstep anything. There is not much harm in it. You can always ask if you are unsure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4150-loki","name":"Loki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T19:51:56-08:00","id":364036,"title":"","content":"So... I totally wasn't expecting to get 8 freaking successes on 9 dice. And I forgot to add it my Artifact Instrument or Hearthstone bonuses. Yikes!<br /> <br /> Why can't I roll like that with my Twilight Archer in the Skype game I'm in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T19:55:39-08:00","id":364038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/361620-clash-of-the-southeast-ooc?p=364036#post364036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I totally wasn't expecting to get 8 freaking successes on 9 dice. And I forgot to add it my Artifact Instrument or Hearthstone bonuses. Yikes!<br /> <br /> Why can't I roll like that with my Twilight Archer in the Skype game I'm in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because Twilights must bear the suffering of a thousand failures for every wonder they bring forth, for that wonder must be the answer to suffering else it is not worthy to be made by their hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T20:16:31-08:00","id":364053,"title":"","content":"My Twilight seems to do okay on the usual Twilight rolls, but if I try to shoot someone with an arrow, I get maybe one success on the same number of dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:32:30-08:00","id":366714,"title":"","content":"&quot;Which way is the restroom?&quot; makes me think super man is about to show up and Klark Kent will miss seeing the superhero once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4157-luxweaver","name":"Luxweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T16:36:37-08:00","id":366717,"title":"","content":"Hey, Swimming Owl just drank a bunch of tea, and this wasn't her first business meeting of the day, nor her first teahouse of the day. It happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T23:26:48-08:00","id":367082,"title":"","content":"Oh god, I am SO sorry!<br /> <br /> I got REALLY busy at work and I completely forgot I submitted for this game.<br /> <br /> It's not too late to play, is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T10:06:30-08:00","id":367482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/361620-clash-of-the-southeast-ooc?p=367082#post367082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god, I am SO sorry!<br /> <br /> I got REALLY busy at work and I completely forgot I submitted for this game.<br /> <br /> It's not too late to play, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It is not. I have all your info. You an start now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4150-loki","name":"Loki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:10:09-08:00","id":367670,"title":"","content":"How long would it take to travel to the Nearest Yu Shan Gate? I'm asking for future reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:06:18-08:00","id":367754,"title":"","content":"Sorry about not posting, I am on the tale end of under the weather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:06:30-08:00","id":367755,"title":"","content":"There are two. The first is directly south approximately 600 miles. The other is the one in nexus which is about 700 miles NNE. That would take about 30 days is walking at a regular pace with plenty of rest. Using a horse with plenty of rest at a normal pace would be about 24 days. If you rushed, you could probably make it there in around 15 days (if you stam+resist could handle it) walking and about 10 days with a horse (if it is kept properly and can handle it; as well as you). If you had horses with replacements and you can handle too (stam+resist) roll, you could easily make it there in 9-10 days. Nexus would take a few days longer.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4150-loki","name":"Loki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:18:54-08:00","id":367770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/361620-clash-of-the-southeast-ooc?p=367754#post367754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry about not posting, I am on the tale end of under the weather.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope you feel better! Don't worry about it too much.<br /> <br /> I am not feeling very well today either. :/ That time of year I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4150-loki","name":"Loki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:05:11-08:00","id":367809,"title":"","content":"Should I be asking my question about the Dragon blooded here in the OCC topic instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:54:33-08:00","id":367857,"title":"","content":"You can do so in the IC thread if you wish. Just make sure it is a part of your dialogue or thoughts or added as an [OOC] extra below your text. You can ask here as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4150-loki","name":"Loki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:26:44-08:00","id":367950,"title":"","content":"so i realized i have lacked to describe my character. He is currently not in his true form and hopes never<br /> to be.<br /> <br /> My true physical appearance: The Servent: My true form is an 85 year old man. With wrinkled leather like skin that bares the marks of countless strikes of the whip and beating of the suns wrath. What little remains of his wispy white hair is slicked back. His brown eyes set deep in a gaunt face tell of uncommon depth and conviction gained only from witnessing atrocities. His hunched bearing is that of a wise man. One would expect the wisdom of an age to pour forth whenever he spoke. His liver spotted body is generally covered by an outfit you\u2019d expect a particularly poor peasant would wear. He has no time for the finery and will be in the nude if he must, although that tends to draw to much attention.<br /> <br /> Current form: Fovnag: A youngster of only 50. He was a master thaumaturge before The Servant ate him to take his form and his manes/town. He wears a gray tunic of light wear lined with silk and well fitted sandals. He rarely gos anywhere without his walking staff made from the heart wood of a palm tree. His features are non descriptive just another average face from the average masses. Only his age is noticeable, less since he has always wears a turban around his balding head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4157-luxweaver","name":"Luxweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:34:35-08:00","id":367976,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Exaltation wipe away most physical imperfections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:49:28-08:00","id":367985,"title":"","content":"It can. But it doesn't have to. The Bull of the North still has his gray/white hair and beard, for instance, even if he's no longer all wrinkly, and I doubt exaltation shrinks your nose and/or ears. I think it's more internal: you no longer get arthritis, your hunch from years of bad posture clears up easily and no longer causes back pain, your eyes become clear and no longer nearsighted or afflicted with cataracts, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T17:02:06-08:00","id":367995,"title":"","content":"well now that you ask im not a 100 percentsure. i remember it being said somewhere but i cant find it now. i don't remember it ever being said in the lunner manual at least. i feel it especially appropriate for The Servant to look like he does now as him being so old is part of the reason he exalted in my mind. No one that is a labor slave should live anywhere close to 80. The Servant bears the marks of the things that made him what he is now. This guy should have died 50 years ago if he where not held together by his hatred for slavery and the guild and the fact he does not want to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4157-luxweaver","name":"Luxweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T17:10:08-08:00","id":368001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luxweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/361620-clash-of-the-southeast-ooc?p=367995#post367995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well now that you ask im not a 100 percentsure. i remember it being said somewhere but i cant find it now. i don't remember it ever being said in the lunner manual at least. i feel it especially appropriate for The Servant to look like he does now as him being so old is part of the reason he exalted in my mind. No one that is a labor slave should live anywhere close to 80. The Servant bears the marks of the things that made him what he is now. This guy should have died 50 years ago if he where not held together by his hatred for slavery and the guild and the fact he does not want to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but his new lifespan is many thousands of years, and I don't think he would have to worry about geriatric illness for that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T17:40:29-08:00","id":368049,"title":"","content":"The Servant's character description is mostly cosmetic, so I doubt he has any age related illnesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:02:22-08:00","id":368061,"title":"","content":"Well damn. The IC thread only had four pages when I went to bed last night, and I come home from work to find six. This might take some catching up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:24:30-08:00","id":368074,"title":"","content":"By no means is he a weak old man. He is quite strong and vital. The best why to describe his physique is stringy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4157-luxweaver","name":"Luxweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:50:20-08:00","id":368125,"title":"","content":"Since we are doing character descriptions....<br /> <br /> Flynn is a tall, long limbed man with grey eyes that looks like he is in his mid-twenties. His dirty blond hair is long and wavy. It is usually kept in a tail at the base of his head. He is pretty good looking in spite of the day old stubble he usually has. Many years under the harsh southern sun has turned his fair northern skin tan.<br /> <br /> His dusty travel clothes, though well worn, are in good repair. He wears sandals on his feet and long traveling cloak. His Sanxian case is never far from him, either strapped to his back or sitting next to him.<br /> <br /> If Flynn is not playing his Sanxian, he is always fidgeting with his hands. He has this restless energy that can only be expressed though music. One would think he would be an awkward man with such long arms and legs, but he is quiet graceful for his size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-13-2015, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:10:55-08:00","id":368144,"title":"","content":"I described how Splendor appears right now IC, but that is essentially wearing a wrap of the cloaks some of the gods with him.<br /> <br /> Under the cloak he is very under-dressed for the South, wearing only a robe of thin silk. He appears about thirty, his hair is prematurely grey and his skin is as pale as if he had never been in direct sunlight. He could almost be said to look washed out. (A result of that incident when he was young.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:11:49-08:00","id":368146,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For convenience's sake...<br /> <br /> Nahuel\u2019s true human form is six feet of lean, bronze-skinned muscle, accented by swirling moonsilver tattoos. He dresses as the jungle tribesman he is, usually with only a brief kilt-like garment around his loins, with perhaps a cloak if the weather is truly inclement. His face could be described as brutally handsome, sharp planed with high cheekbones, a strong jaw, and brilliant greenish-yellow eyes with slitted pupils.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T03:57:59-08:00","id":368508,"title":"","content":"Since we're doing character descriptions, I whipped up a quick character portrait for Swimming Owl. Not really sure my technical chops are up to &quot;Appearance 4&quot; portraiture, but the idea's there.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://th07.deviantart.net/fs71/PRE/f/2015/013/9/5/swimming_owl_portrait_by_flyingspiderstudios-d8dqgka.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Not shown in this picture: The bottoms of her steel boots and the dirt and grime from a couple of weeks of caravan travel.","signature